Defect O1: BRepOffsetAPI_ThruSections::Generated() fails on a ruled loft through
sections that are each one closed edge.

Defect id: O1 (pySMESH defect sweep 4.2.2, sections 9 O1 and 13.3).

Symptom: a ruled loft (ruled = true) through 4 or more sections, each one closed edge
(a circle, a closed spline), builds. Generated() of any section vertex then throws
NCollection_IndexedDataMap::FindFromKey. BRepTools_History(args, maker) calls
Generated() for every sub-shape, so the history of the loft cannot be built at all.
With 3 sections it does not throw, but it returns a section edge in place of the
second longitudinal edge.

Root cause: in the vertex branch of Generated(), ruled mode, the walk along the
chain of longitudinal edges picks the next edge by its position in the
vertex-to-edge list of a face: First() or Last(), whichever is not the current
edge. A section of one closed edge makes every ruled face periodic. The face then
holds its longitudinal edge twice (a seam, FORWARD and REVERSED), and the closed
section edge carries the vertex at both of its ends. First() and Last() can be the
same seam edge, or the section edge, so the walk stalls on a stale vertex. The next
face does not contain that vertex, and FindFromKey throws.

Change: the next longitudinal edge is the edge of the next face at the current
vertex that is not degenerated and not an edge of the section between the two
faces. The same rule already selects the next edge in the degenerated-section
branch of this function. A missing edge throws Standard_DomainError instead of
returning a null shape.

Files and functions changed:
  src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKOffset/BRepOffsetAPI/BRepOffsetAPI_ThruSections.cxx
    BRepOffsetAPI_ThruSections::Generated(), vertex branch, ruled chain walk.

Applies to: OCCT V8_0_1 (b8f597c677811d1f9f4d8a97f5ae2825c0353a42).

